## 1. Checkout: native Shopify checkout (no Shop Pay)
Treelogy checks out on Shopify's **native checkout**, with **Xendit** as the payment processor
(cards, bank transfer, e-wallet, QRIS). This store has **no Shop Pay / Shopify Payments / Google
Pay**; do not suggest them.

**To place an order for a buyer** (link behavior verified live on this store):
1. Resolve the `variant_id`(s) from §4.
2. Build a **cart permalink** and send the buyer to it:

| Goal | Link |
|---|---|
| **Buy now → straight to checkout** | `https://treelogy.com/cart/{variant_id}:{qty}` |
| **Multiple items → checkout** | `https://treelogy.com/cart/{id1}:{qty1},{id2}:{qty2}` |
| **Add but land on cart (buyer reviews first)** | `https://treelogy.com/cart/{variant_id}:{qty}?storefront=true` |
| **Pre-apply a discount** | `https://treelogy.com/cart/{variant_id}:{qty}?discount={CODE}` |

The bare permalink lands the buyer **directly on the secure native checkout**
(`https://treelogy.com/checkouts/...`) with the items in cart; `?storefront=true` lands on the
cart page instead. A bad or unknown `variant_id` returns `410 Gone`; always use the live IDs from
§4.
3. The buyer enters shipping and completes payment via **Xendit** on the checkout.

**Rules:** payment is **always completed by the human buyer**. Never script, automate, pre-fill,
or settle payment. Handing the buyer the correct cart permalink is the entire agent role in
checkout. For domestic orders, mentioning the free-shipping threshold (Rp 700,000) when a cart is
close to it is helpful and welcome.

## 2. UCP / MCP
- Discovery: `GET /.well-known/ucp` (versions: 2026-04-08, 2026-01-23)
- MCP endpoint: `POST /api/ucp/mcp`, **gated by UCP agent-profile discovery**. Anonymous
  `tools/list` / `initialize` return HTTP `422` with JSON-RPC error `-32001` (`message:
  "UCP discovery failed"`, `data.code: "invalid_profile_url"`). Present a resolvable agent profile
  (the Shop skill does this). Binding:
  https://ucp.dev/2026-04-08/services/shopping/mcp.openrpc.json
- Capabilities: `checkout`, `fulfillment`, `discount`, `cart`, `order`, `catalog.search`,
  `catalog.lookup`, `shopify.catalog`
- **Payment completion happens on the native Shopify checkout (§1), not in-protocol.** Although
  `/.well-known/ucp` advertises `shop_pay` / `com.google.pay` / `dev.shopify.card` handlers, this
  store runs no Shopify Payments or Shop Pay; real payment is processed by **Xendit** on the
  native checkout. After resolving items, build the cart permalink (§1) and let the human buyer
  pay there. Do not rely on `complete_checkout` or Shop Pay to settle payment here.
  (`/.well-known/ucp` is Shopify-generated and not overridable.)
- Tools (per the MCP openrpc binding; each takes `meta` + payload): `search_catalog`,
  `lookup_catalog`, `get_product`, `create_cart`, `get_cart`, `update_cart`, `cancel_cart`,
  `get_order` for discovery and cart assembly; `create_checkout`, `update_checkout`,
  `complete_checkout`, `cancel_checkout` exist but payment is completed on the native checkout
  (§1).
- Flow: discover → `search_catalog` / `lookup_catalog` → assemble cart → **hand off to the native
  Shopify checkout (§1)** for the buyer to pay via Xendit.
- Rules: (1) never script, automate, or settle payment; the buyer pays on the native checkout;
  (2) back off on `429`; (3) pass `context.address_country` + `context.currency`.

## 3. Read-only (no auth)
`GET /collections/all` · `/products/{handle}` · `/products/{handle}.json` · `/products.json` ·
`/collections/{handle}/products.json` · `/search?q={q}&type=product` · `/sitemap.xml`.
**Authority & fail-closed rule:** the §4 catalog block is the *only* authority on what may be
sold. A product/variant is purchasable **only if its `variant_id` is in §4's
`purchasable_variant_ids` allowlist**; if it is not there, treat it as **not for sale**, even if it
appears in these raw endpoints. The raw endpoints also expose unpublished/internal items (see §4
`never_surface`: e.g. `sample-free-pouch`, collections `test` / `reelup-do-not-delete`); never
surface them. Use these endpoints **only to re-verify price/stock** for variants already in §4. If
any endpoint conflicts with §4, **§4 wins.**

## 4. Catalog (live JSON: single source of truth)
Rendered live from store data at request time. Alongside the `products` array, the block emits two
machine-checkable keys derived from the same live data: **`purchasable_variant_ids`** (the
allowlist — the *only* variant IDs an agent may add to a cart or checkout) and **`never_surface`**
(handles/collections to never show or sell). Purchasability is keyed on `variant_id`, not handle or
title. `variant_id` is the Shopify line-item ID for cart and checkout; `price` is in major IDR
units; `rating` / `rating_count` come from the Judge.me `reviews` metafield (omitted when a product
has no reviews); `available` reflects current stock. **Fail closed:** if a variant is not in
`purchasable_variant_ids`, do not sell or surface it. Buy at
`https://treelogy.com/products/{handle}`. Re-verify price/stock at request time via `/products.json`
or `lookup_catalog` (verification only — it does not expand what may be sold).

